## 🐧 Linux USB Permissions (Udev Rule)

To access the WebHID / USB device directly under Linux without `sudo` (root) privileges, you need to run the following udev rule in the terminal once:

```bash
echo 'SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="0c45", ATTR{idProduct}=="800a", MODE="0666"' | sudo tee /etc/udev/rules.d/99-aula.rules
sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger

```

> **Important:** Make sure your keyboard is connected to the computer via a USB Type-C cable. HID configuration commands may be hardware-restricted in 2.4G wireless or Bluetooth mode.

