## 🛠️ OS-Specific Build (Desktop Build)

The application can be compiled directly for your operating system as a standalone desktop application.

### Prerequisites

* [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (Version 18 or above; Node 20 / 22 / 24)
* `npm` package manager
* **FUSE 2 Library for Linux (`fuse2` / `libfuse2`)**: It is **mandatory** to have the `fuse2` package installed on your system so that AppImage packages can be run directly by double-clicking:
* **Arch Linux / Manjaro:** `sudo pacman -S fuse2`
* **Ubuntu / Debian / Linux Mint:** `sudo apt install libfuse2`
* **Fedora / RHEL:** `sudo dnf install fuse-libs`
* **openSUSE:** `sudo zypper install libfuse2`



```bash
# Clone the project and enter the directory
git clone https://github.com/nopickart/f108-pro-web-gui-app.git
cd f108-pro-web-gui-app

# Install dependencies
npm install

```

---

### 1. Build for Linux (.AppImage & .deb)

Generates an `.AppImage` to **run by double-clicking** on your Linux desktop and a `.deb` package to install on your system:

```bash
# Install Electron build tools
npm install -D electron electron-builder

# Build Linux packages
npm run dist:linux

```

When the build is complete, the outputs are created in the **`release/`** folder:

* **`release/Aula F108 Pro Controller-1.0.0.AppImage`**
* **`release/aula-f108-pro_1.0.0_amd64.deb`**

#### Running by Double-Clicking on the Desktop:

1. Move the `.AppImage` file in the `release/` folder to your Desktop.
2. Right-click the file: **Properties → Permissions → Check the "Allow executing file as program" box** (or `chmod +x ~/Desktop/*.AppImage` from the terminal).
3. **Double-click the icon**, and the application will open in a native, standalone desktop window!

> ⚠️ **Mandatory Requirement (FUSE 2):**
> For AppImage packages to be opened by double-clicking on Linux systems, the `fuse2` package must be installed:
> * **Arch Linux:** `sudo pacman -S fuse2`
> * **Ubuntu / Debian:** `sudo apt install libfuse2`
> * **Fedora:** `sudo dnf install fuse-libs`
> *(If you want to run it directly without installing FUSE: `./release/*.AppImage --appimage-extract-and-run`)*
> 
> 

If you want to install it as a system application on Debian/Ubuntu/Linux Mint:

```bash
sudo dpkg -i release/aula-f108-pro_1.0.0_amd64.deb

```

---

### 2. Build for Windows (.exe Setup & Portable)

Generates a one-click installation wizard (`Setup.exe`) and a double-clickable portable (`portable.exe`) package that requires no installation for Windows:

```bash
npm run dist:win

```

Outputs are located in the **`release/`** folder:

* **`release/Aula F108 Pro Controller Setup 1.0.0.exe`**
* **`release/Aula F108 Pro Controller 1.0.0.exe`** (Portable)

---

### 3. Build for macOS (.dmg)

Generates a disk image (`.dmg`) for macOS that you can directly mount and install:

```bash
npm run dist:mac

```

Output is located in the **`release/`** folder:

* **`release/Aula F108 Pro Controller-1.0.0.dmg`**

